  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_016 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) achieved 0.527 acc / 0.510 F1, a clear +4.2% improvement over the rna_only baseline (config_001, 0.485 acc). This confirms that adding the image modality is beneficial. Question: Does moving from singleprofile to multiprofile (with avgpool aggregation) further improve performance while keeping the same RNA encoder, image encoder, and fusion strategy? This is a direct, single-axis extension of the best configuration so far. Rationale: With only two experiments completed, the largest unexplored design axis is profile setting (single vs. multi). Multiprofile captures richer temporal/dynamic information and could yield a gain comparable to the modality addition. config_018 isolates this change cleanly (only profile_setting and aggregation differ from config_016), making attribution straightforward. If multiprofile helps, it opens the aggregation-strategy sub-axis (avgpool vs. transformer) for further exploitation; if it does not, we can confidently redirect budget toward fusion strategy or alternative encoders. This is the highest-information-per-experiment choice under the limited budget."
}

